A||N||3||opm2000||'86 block into '88 ?||||1||
Z||000000||opm2000||01-07-2001||07:33 AM||||Gang,<BR>      For a lack of anything better to do, I have been considering taking the '86 v6 engine which I have setting around, and sticking it into my '88 formula which has a rod-knocked engine.   Questions are...will this be a fairly straightforward install?<P>   I'm talking about taking only the '86 engine, and putting it into the '88 cradle, engine wiring harness, & 5-spd transmission.<P>   Does anyone know if the '86 flywheel will bolt up to the clutch for the '88 ?   <P>David Breeze<BR>N777H<BR>'84 4cyl/4spd....still running<BR>'85 v6/4spd......parts & more parts<BR>'86 v6/auto......rebuilt everything<BR>'87 v6/5spd......newly acquired, thanx Gokart<BR>'88 v6/5spd......87K mi w/rod knock||||reg||1
Z||000001||88formula||01-07-2001||09:44 AM||||I think the motor is a straight blot in but the 88 flywheel cannot be used in the 86 motor. The 86 motor is externally balanced and the 88 motor is internally balanced. That means that the 86 motor needs a flywheel with a counterweight on it and the 88 motor has a neutrally balanced flywheel.||||reg||1
Z||000002||opm2000||01-07-2001||11:10 AM||||[QUOTE]Originally posted by 88formula:<BR> the 86 motor needs a flywheel with a counterweight on it and the 88 motor has a neutrally balanced flywheel<P>Yep, Knowing that, I have to "bolt-in" the entire '86 motor...from the harmonic balancer in front---to the flywheel in back.<P>Now the only question is will the '86 flywheel accept the clutch plate used by the '88 5spd transmission ?   ie. are the holes there to bolt it on ?<P>I've assumed I can bolt the arm which goes with the '88 front engine mount...directly onto the '86 block with no problems, thereby fitting onto the '88 cradle just fine.   And I've assumed the '88 engine harness will plug right up to the various connections on the '86 engine, as well.<P>Once I seperate the engines from their transmissions, I will quickly find out, but I plan on painting the '84 4cyl & '86 auto first, this spring.   That means engine seperation doesn't happen till mid-summer.   <P>David Breeze<BR>N777H <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/viking300a/FrameSet1.html" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/viking300a/FrameSet1.html</A> <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||01-07-2001||05:53 PM||||Well I don't know for sure by I assume that if the guys here that bolt up the 5-speed Getrag/Muncie transmissions to their 85-86 fiero's can do it you can too.||||reg||1
